    "body": "Adaptive and linear curriculum are both implemented, but adaptive currently produces high variance across runs and does not reliably learn to trot due to being \"too cautious\", i.e. not allowing a temporary decrease in performance to get out of the hopping local minimum. Still investigating, but it's definitely better than without so it's a good point to merge into main. \r\n\r\nAlso various improvements in evaluation script and plot generation",
